    "body": "These are several agent fixes/enhancements which came up in trials generating user-defined livelits with the agent. \r\n\r\n- The biggest one was decreasing parse time for large code insertions, enabled by #2426 which this is stacked on.\r\n- Better agent probing: Previously the agent probe action did not wait for the worker to return, requiring a multi-round potentially race-conditiony process to actually see probed values. Now waits before sending results to model; checks in 150ms beats until the eval result settles (bounded ~10s). \r\n- Chat storage is reworked around per-chat records (a fresh agent's persisted state drops from ~152KB to ~2KB); these could get quite large and effect agent latency\r\n- The edit tools plus view/probe tools address module members through owner/member paths\r\n- funlet fix supporting `let f(x) = e` paths for modules\r\n- Stubbed read_docs doc-pack registry which will be populated in user-livelits; this enables breaking up the system prompt into on-demand docs files\r\n\n\n---\n### Fixes brought over from the aria-demo branch (2026-09-09)\nSix independent one-commit fixes, ~105 lines total. Each was verified to be a dev-level problem before landing here (details in the commit messages).\n- d398436869 Menhir: `Int(x)`-style patterns (type-keyword constructors) no longer fall back to the slow parser.\n- c704c8149f + 84fd46f42c Worker: the reuse pre-pass ran twice per request and every node paid a reuse check; now once, and only above 2500 statics entries. Drag-to-result on a ~100-line program went 2.0 s \u2192 0.2 s.\n- 0953ad542b Projector commits (slider, checkbox, livelit gestures) skip the 225 ms typing debounce.\n- 6c1d1a930d Probe All: ambient samples capture no environment (was ~80% of retained heap; worker 1.8 GB \u2192 186 MB on a 150-line program).\n- 8afaf6dfd4 Follow-up to the above, easy to drop: placing a probe under Probe All re-evaluates so the new probe's context menu still shows bindings.\n",
